e latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 50% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 67% and a beta of 1.21, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 2.68 vs 5y 1.38), so read it loosely.","About $82.1M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 31% in the 2020 crash, 39% in the 2022 bear market and 43% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $14.12 (margin of safety -433%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 61%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 30.8 vs 22.1 and EV/EBITDA 18.1 vs 12.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 28% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 2.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 4 covering analysts target $118 on average, 56% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 20% clears the cost of capital of 11.0% by 9pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.26).","Earnings quality is a concern: a weak Piotroski score of 2/9 and cash conversion of only 0.00x.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 4.0% of revenue on R&D and 1.2% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 6.9, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.63).","Working capital ties up about 132 days of sales, a drag on cash generation.","The Beneish M-score (-2.05) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 17.5% over 3 years, 22.9% over 5 years and 14.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","Free cash flow has compounded -14.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 441%.","Capex runs 1.5x depreciation (6.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own 16.7%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 87%.","Insider trading is two-way: 2 purchases and 8 sales over the past year, net $10.7M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.5% (0.5% in dividends).","The share count has grown 0.9% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 20 consecutive years, raising it 10.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 5,897 employees, each generates about $245K of revenue, 0.7x the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 12.8% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $975K (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":66,"head":"Avoid: priced 433% above its fair value of $14.12.","pros":["Composite 40, above the 39 line (gates 11/26)","ROIC 20.1% vs WACC 11.0%","Revenue grew 22.9%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.0x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 433% above fair value of $14.12","Piotroski F-score 2/9","P/E 30.8x vs sector 22.1x","EV/EBITDA 18.1x vs sector 12.9x"],"flags":["Priced 433% above its fair value of $14.12"],"need":[],"buy_below":12.0,"vc":{"base":14.12,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":14.12,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.6059,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (61% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"ticker":"AAON","date":"2026-11-20"}